2186296955 1089 "q-136018" 13194139534582 true] [17592186296955 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534582 true] [17592186296955 1100 "The coefficient of ${b}^{4}$ in the expansion of ${(1-\\frac{b}{3})}^{9}$ is" 13194139534582 true] [17592186296955 1113 #uuid "c07d4a9d-1a61-586f-93cb-62583b04cc4f" 13194139534582 true] [17592186296955 1145 "The binomial expansion for $(1+x)^{n}$ is given by\n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}{x}^{2}+⋯.\n$$\n\nIn particular, the ${x}^{4}$ term is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{n(n-1)(n-2)(n-3)}{4!}{x}^{4}.\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $-\\frac{b}{3}$ and $n$ with $9$ in the above expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9(9-1)(9-2)(9-3)}{4!}\\cdot {(-\\frac{b}{3})}^{4} & =\\frac{9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6}{24}\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{3})}^{4}\\cdot {b}^{4} \\\\  & =126\\cdot \\frac{1}{81}{b}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{9}{b}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${b}^{4}$ is $\\frac{14}{9}.$" 13194139534582 true] [17592186296956 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296957 13194139534582 true] [17592186296956 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296958 13194139534582 true] [17592186296956 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296959 13194139534582 true] [17592186296956 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296960 13194139534582 true] [17592186296956 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296961 13194139534582 true] [17592186296956 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534582 true] [17592186296956 1041 "selection" 13194139534582 true] [17592186296956 1104 #edb/ref 17592186296960 13194139534582 true] [17592186296956 1110 #uuid "730a087b-4bb9-5755-8f76-d5caf8022a24" 13194139534582 true] [17592186296957 1034 "-\\frac{28}{9}" 13194139534582 true] [17592186296957 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534582 true] [17592186296957 1111 #uuid "de0723b8-de73-5adf-9f76-9a7a5d685cb1" 13194139534582 true] [17592186296958 1034 "\\frac{28}{9}" 13194139534582 true] [17592186296958 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534582 true] [17592186296958 1111 #uuid "765beb4f-575b-542e-b47c-62de78e681b0" 13194139534582 true] [17